# Applied in this order with 'patch -p1' on vanilla Linux $(KERNEL_VERSION).
# Source: psx-place patch set by Sombat Tragoongoson, via github.com/damiandudycz/ps3 (files/kernel-patches/.../6.12).
# Authors (restored 2026-10-21 from the copyright lines; the source patches carry no headers): ps3/0010-0270 are
# glevand's OtherOS++ set (graf_chokolo co-author where his copyright is), 0280-0450 later psx-place fixes whose
# author isn't recorded; each patch's From: and Origin: say which. local/: ours, or the upstream author kept.
# 0010 is refreshed for 6.12.112 (one hunk dropped, already fixed upstream) and must come after the others.
# 0030 adds /dev/ps3gpu_* (GPU FIFO/ctrl/VRAM access); disabled in Gentoo's 6.12 set, builds fine here.
# local/ holds our own fixes on top. local/0020-0032 are other people's fixes (authors kept): gelic
# and ps3 spu from upstream after 6.12, spufs fixes posted to linuxppc-dev but not merged (2026-08);
# survey and sources in docs/OTHEROS-PATCHES.md.
# Dropped 2026-10-18 (same file): ps3/0060 (/dev/ps3sysmngr), 0090 (ps3rom vendor commands), 0160 (ps3jupiter),
# 0170 (gelic eurus repository write), 0316 (jupiter alias). local/0040 no longer needs the misc device.
# local/0040: SM temperatures as hwmon; 0041: the final shutdown poll waits for the SM's shutdown command (docs/THERMAL.md).
# local/0042: fan policy through the SM (hwmon pwm1; SYSCON automatic at boot and on every exit path; docs/THERMAL.md).
# local/0043: ps3fb frees its console's XDR frame (8 MiB) while ps3rsx owns the GPU; ps3fb.shadow_release=1, default off (docs/KERNEL-MEMORY.md 6).
# local/0045: ps3disk write guard: ps3da read-only, ps3db writable only inside the ranges sealed in /sys/block/ps3db/write_guard/ (docs/GAMEOS-HDD.md "The kernel guard").
#   On since 2026-10-19: ps3-imgmap-boot create (the SSD root's initramfs) and ps3-imgmap create (Phase A) register and seal their dm tables' ranges;
#   every other write to ps3db fails. Phase A on a kernel with it needs the new tools/ssdimg/ps3-imgmap on the PS3.
# local/0046: one hcall per hash table insertion instead of two (ps3_htab.insert_readback=0; default 1, the old read-back;
#   2 compares both) and htab hcall stats in /sys/module/ps3_htab/parameters/stats (docs/HOTPATHS.md "Soft-masked time").
# local/0048: ps3disk (ps3/0010) probe error unwind (unsigned loop index) and remove order (gendisk[] pointers cleared under the lock, free_irq before the DMA region).
# local/0047: snd_ps3 restarts a DMA chain whose buffer-empty interrupts stopped (snd_ps3.dma_watchdog_ms=200, 0 off; the
#   OpenAL "Wait timeout" wedge) and counts interrupts by kind in /sys/module/snd_ps3/parameters/dma_stats (docs/games/LOG-FINDINGS.md 1).
# local/0049: gelic re-probes itself when the wired port has link and sends but receives nothing (ps3_gelic.rx_watchdog=0 off;
#   ps3_gelic.rx_watchdog_test=N simulates N faults; docs/release/TESTING-0.1.md 22).
# local/0050: hid-sony starts the DS3's sticks centered (128), not at 0 (fully up/left) until the pad's first report; an
#   inactive pad on the cable ran Quake's menu up by itself (linux/tests/sixaxis-idle-axes.sh, ds3-idle-check.py on the PS3).
# local/0051: ps3fb's graph exception dump prints the 32 FIFO cache entries ending at GET, GET and PUT marked, rate-limited
#   (docs/RSX.md "Reading ps3fb's dump").
